    "created_at": "2026-02-17T09:44:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-17T14:15:11Z",
    "body": "If you add something like `a + s = b` with slack variable `s`, and indicator constraints `z = 1 -> s >= 0`, `z = 0 -> s <= 0` with a binary variable `z`, then `z=1` means `b - a >= 0`, so `a <= b`, and `z=0` means `b - a <= 0`, so `b <= a`. Changing some 0 to 1e-5 may give a better distinction around `a=b`.",
